12
01:05:41,052 --> 01:05:47,052
Trust (stylized as trust_) is a 2010 American drama thriller film directed by David Schwimmer and
written by Andy Bellin and Robert Festinger based on an uncredited story by Schwimmer.

13
01:11:09,473 --> 01:11:15,473
Starring Clive Owen, Catherine Keener, Jason Clarke, Liana Liberato, and Viola Davis, the film follows a fourteen-year-old
girl who becomes a victim of sexual abuse after meeting a man posing as a teenage boy on an online chat room.

14
01:16:37,894 --> 01:16:43,894
Trust premiered at the Toronto International Film Festival on September 10, 2010, and was
given a limited theatrical release in the United States on April 1, 2011.

15
01:22:06,315 --> 01:22:12,315
The film received positive reviews, with Liberato's
performance earning critical praise.

16
01:27:34,736 --> 01:27:40,736
Liberato won the Silver Hugo Award for Best Actress at the Chicago International Film Festival, and
Schwimmer was nominated for the Grand Special Prize at the Deauville American Film Festival.

17
01:33:03,157 --> 01:33:09,157
The film explores themes of pedophilia, high
school, child abuse, rape, sexual abuse.

18
01:38:31,578 --> 01:38:37,578
The tone is emotional and intense.
